While we're at it, let me add another related story - about a stupid
death, that is, in my case...

Also at Medusa in her circular island in the mid of the sea. I spotted
two scrolls, one on each of two islands on the east. Bridged the water
with cold, and just at the moment when I intended to come close to the
ice-bridge some monster came around the corner of Medusa's home to zap
that wand of fire at me. Well, lucky me, I turned to kill him quickly,
got his wand of fire and rebuilt the ice bridge. I think to remember
that I reached the first island and picked up the scroll. Built another
ice bridge to the next island. And while I was in the midst of the
bridge a very good hidden (blue in blue; I always miss to notice them)
water troll zapped another wand of fire at me.

It's as always in Nethack; you usually never encounter wands of fire
at Medusa's level, but once you intend to use the unsafe ice-bridge,
and you've even been warned once, there's another one applied against
you shortly after, and exactly at the moment when there's no solid
ground near.

I learned the hard way that the adjacent ice was not sufficient to get
onto a safe square (or was it some 1 in 10 chance that I lost grip?),
and my otherwise invincible character drowned. Killed by the most
terrible creature in Nethack; the one behind the keyboard! <sigh>

